1. How to Split Wide Tables Across the 3 Pages
With many columns in FACT_ATTENDANCE, DIM_TICKET_DIVISION_CATEGORY, and your calendar table, split fields by purpose instead of cramming everything onto one screen:
 * Main Dashboard (Attendance_USJ — Executive & Operational View): Show only the 5 core KPI cards (Total Attendance, Unique Tickets, Active Ticket Divisions, Average Daily Attendance, Attendance Days), calendar period attributes (THIS_YEAR_DATE, YEAR_MONTH, YEAR_QUARTER, YEAR_WEEK_ID, WEEK_END_DATE, WEEKEND_FLAG), and ticket division labels—never raw surrogate keys (DATE_ID, TICKET_DIVISION_KEY) or audit/technical columns.
 * Detail Page (Detailed Info — Granular Drill-Down): Put full tabular/matrix breakdowns by date, week, year-month, and ticket division attributes so analysts or operations leads can inspect underlying numbers without cluttering the overview.
 * Glossary Page (Glossary — Definitions & Governance): Document every KPI formula, ticket division rule, calendar period definition (THIS_YEAR_DATE, YEAR_WEEK_ID, WEEK_END_DATE), and refresh/grain note in a clean reference table.
2. Which "Advanced" Power BI Visuals Are Worth Adding (and Which to Skip)
Stick to native Power BI visuals (and clean DAX measures) so your .pbip project stays fast, portable, and free of third-party custom visual approval headaches:
| Visual / Feature | Worth Adding? | Why It Helps End Users & Seniors |
|---|---|---|
| New Card Visual + Reference Labels | Yes | Displays the 5 core KPIs cleanly in one container with built-in comparison/target labels instead of separate text boxes. |
| Line & Clustered Column (Combo Chart) | Yes | Lets users compare attendance volume bars against a trend or rolling average line across YEAR_MONTH or YEAR_WEEK_ID. |
| Small Multiples | Yes | Repeats the same trend chart across ticket divisions or calendar slices side by side so spikes and drops stand out immediately. |
| Dynamic DAX + Field Parameters | Yes | Lets users switch metrics or period granularity dynamically using standard Power BI visuals rather than fragile custom JSON tricks. |
| Scatter / Waterfall / Decomposition Tree | Optional | Use only if you have a clear variance/driver question—keep the landing page focused and put deep explorers on Detailed Info or a dedicated tab. |
| Heavy R/Python or Unverified Custom Visuals | Skip | Slower rendering, potential corporate/tenant restrictions, and extra maintenance overhead for teammates. |
